[32m+[m[32m## ❓ FAQ[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### Q: Why use React.memo instead of useMemo?[m
[32m+[m[32m**A:** React.memo memoizes the entire component, preventing unnecessary re-renders. useMemo is for values. For components with expensive renders, memo is better.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### Q: How does request deduplication work?[m
[32m+[m[32m**A:** If two components request the same data simultaneously, we cache the first promise and return it to the second. Both get the same result from one API call.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### Q: Why 500ms debounce for search?[m
[32m+[m[32m**A:** 500ms provides a good balance between responsiveness and API efficiency. It's fast enough for user feedback but prevents excessive requests.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### Q: What about SEO impact of lazy loading?[m
[32m+[m[32m**A:** Images below the fold are lazy loaded, which is fine for SEO. Critical images use priority={true}. Search engines handle lazy loading well.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### Q: How do I validate the performance improvements?[m
[32m+[m[32m**A:** Use Lighthouse audit before/after, check DevTools Profiler, measure Core Web Vitals, and monitor API call counts.[m
